From 7a359856117413fc1e7c3e9946b9df35710431f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: desocketed <desocketed@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 22:32:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] vk_exec: NX2NAVI_EVO_ASYNC=1 runs the ambient occlusion again
 after the event it waits for when the replay runs on its own thread (default
 1; 0 = submission order) (#146)

Upstream's event order across queues (3aa8ff5) turns itself off under
NX2NAVI_REPLAY_ASYNC=1, so the worker queue's occlusion read the previous
frame's depth again (play24 e1fbd67 flicker, dump f17378). Port of our 0046
(AO_ORDER) onto the rebase: unmet top-level waits are noted with the queue
state, and at the signal that makes one hold the binds and the occlusion chain
dispatches after it run once more. The async submit keeps recordings with a
wait alive 64 more submissions. The occlusion compute's hash under the rebase
translator (59867f7d) is added, which also revives NX2NAVI_AO=0.
